Emerald 3DS changes to pret/pokeemerald 76463dac15cad36aca5e2b3f6366abf9e53f814f: Japanese naming screen keyboard
Applies after 0059-japanese-name-length.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

The Japanese ROM's naming screen: hiragana, katakana and a Latin page of 19 keys a row,
whose characters are the keys' text (staged as the gText_NamingScreenKeyboard_* rows);
the player's name and Walda's phrase start on hiragana, Pokémon and box names on
katakana. The dakuten and handakuten keys and R (the next form of the last character,
from two tables staged into this file) change the last character. Characters are 10
pixels apart, with the ROM's positions for the cursor, text, underscores, titles,
gender sign and controls; the kana page labels are two tiles. Walda's phrase takes 12
characters. tools/localize_japanese.py stages the keyboard graphics only into a tree
with this patch (it looks for NAMING_SCREEN_KANA).

